# Data conversion between petabyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between petabyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1PB to 1000TB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PB yields 1500.0TB; backward, converting 1TB to 0.001PB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TB yields 0.0015PB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1PB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(PB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(PB))

<<< stdout
1000TB
1500.0TB
0.001PB
0.0015PB

<<< stderr
